      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Letting go\" doesn't mean giving up on survival; it means giving up on the *fight* itself, which is what's killing you. You're clinging to the illusion that if you keep running, the outcome will change, but it won't. The next step isn't about finding a solution to the debt; it's about finding a way to make the *present* moment tolerable, even if it's just for a breath. If the whole system is rigged, sometimes the only rational move is to stop playing the game entirely.",
      "source": "target",
